## 6. COMMON ERRORS

| Error | Solution |
|---|---|
| `mvn: command not found` | `sudo apt install maven -y` |
| JAR file not found | Run `mvn clean package` |
| Main class not found | Check `mainClass` in pom.xml |
| Git command error | Install Git plugin |
| Repository not found | Check GitHub URL |
| Permission denied | Check Jenkins workspace permissions |
| No Pipeline option | Install Pipeline plugin |

## RESULT

Thus, a Jenkins Continuous Delivery pipeline was created to automatically retrieve source code from GitHub, build the Java application, package it into a JAR file, deploy it to a separate directory and execute the deployed application.

**Remember:** Experiments 15–18 have the same CD procedure. Only the Java program and execution arguments change.
